1
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:16,320
Bangkok...

2
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,680
has a lot in common with me.

3
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:23,920
It's a metropolis built on pure hedonism,

4
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:25,480
dripping in opulence.

5
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,440
It's where you live as if tomorrow doesn't exist,

6
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:42,000
yet beneath that facade, no one knows...

7
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,000
what ambition actually looks like.

8
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,120
Now, this boxer in the blue corner

9
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:51,920
has quite an impressive background.

10
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:54,760
He's the son of a politician.

11
00:00:57,160 --> 00:00:58,800
The "Perfect Face,"

12
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:01,840
Yok Pruttha.

13
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:03,920
Yok Pruttha...

14
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:04,599
He's the minister's...

15
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:05,160
[Minister Pongpaisan Sukonsiri]

16
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:05,680
[Minister of Sports]

17
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:12,440
And we're off.

18
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,560
Round one.

19
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:26,640
In Bangkok,

20
00:01:28,039 --> 00:01:30,120
success isn't about how much money you have,

21
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,720
but how much time you can afford to have.

22
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:36,560
Araya Group doesn't just build skyscrapers.

23
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:37,600
We're creating

24
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,000
the "Bangkok Time Solution,"

25
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,640
a way for you to curate

26
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:41,800
your own time in this city.

27
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:46,080
I don't look at customer data on paper.

28
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:48,160
I look at the person

29
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:49,240
behind the data.

30
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,800
Whether it's a father...

31
00:01:53,520 --> 00:01:55,800
who wants to be there for every step of his child's life

32
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:58,600
or a mother...

33
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:02,960
who wants her morning yoga on her own rooftop.

34
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:05,960
It's no different from investing.

35
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,639
Every investor weighs the costs to see...

36
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,880
if the time they put in is worth the return.

37
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,120
Wouldn't you agree?

38
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,760
You live up to your reputation, Tiwakorn Adularaya,

39
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,680
CEO of Araya Group.

40
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,760
But I flew five hours to get here.

41
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,640
I need concrete answers.

42
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,120
What do you give your customers...

43
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:31,360
that makes them willing to put their money down

44
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,480
for this time solution plan?

45
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:35,480
[Match 5, 2:59, Round 3]

46
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:52,880
It's quite simple.

47
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,280
We let the results speak for themselves.

48
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:58,760
Araya Group has officially partnered

49
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,040
with TL Group.

50
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,560
And the results?

51
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,520
Our clients

52
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,880
are willing to pay a 15% premium

53
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:05,920
just so they can get...

54
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,880
two hours of their day back.

55
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,840
I've already finalized things with TL Group.

56
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:17,640
They're ready to promote

57
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:20,480
this Bangkok Time Solution across all channels

58
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:23,240
whether in Beijing, Shanghai, or Guangzhou.

59
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:24,360
Mr. Wirot,

60
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,160
you just spent five hours

61
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:27,240
flying back from Beijing.

62
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:29,480
You know better than anyone

63
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:31,800
how much those two hours are worth,

64
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:35,920
especially when you have the attention of investors

65
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,440
who have the means to pay.

66
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,320
Would you care for another cup of coffee?

67
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,120
What a massive upset

68
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:48,079
in this match.

69
00:03:48,079 --> 00:03:49,640
They've been trading blows.

70
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:52,560
And the winner is...

71
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,280
Yok Pruttha.

72
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,720
This might not be the best time,

73
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:00,960
but there's an update on the Pattaya project.

74
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,520
The soil survey request has been rejected.

75
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,920
They said...

76
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,240
they want a fresh

77
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,320
and more exciting proposal.

78
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,000
They're just putting on a show.

79
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,360
Probably looking for a kickback.

80
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:12,720
That seems to be the case.

81
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,440
There's one more thing.

82
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:17,959
The former Chairman just called me.

83
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:19,760
He insists that you must go back home

84
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,560
for dinner tomorrow.

85
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:24,160
Urgent matters are usually just headaches.

86
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,000
Can I skip it?

87
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:27,760
He said Itt is bringing

88
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:28,800
Phet's younger brother over

89
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,360
as a guest.

90
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,080
-Phet? -Yes.

91
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,720
Mr. Pongpruet Sukonsiri,

92
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,960
a member of the Pattaya City Council.

93
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:41,920
A connection just landed right at my doorstep.

94
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,200
Tell him I'll be there.

95
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,840
I'd like to see his brother for myself.

96
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,680
That left hook was 0.5 seconds too slow.

97
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,720
Is your injury still bothering you?

98
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:55,560
-He won the fight -Sorry.

99
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,800
and donated the prize money to orphans,

100
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:01,400
the poor, and the underprivileged.

101
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:06,120
Alright, Miss Piang.

102
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,320
It's time for me,

103
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,080
your secretary, to clock out.

104
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:12,040
Please don't send me any work while I'm off.

105
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,520
This secretary is going to have some fun.

106
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,160
Bye.

107
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,520
A secretary leaving before the CEO

108
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,280
is unacceptable,

109
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,280
Mr. Ing.

110
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:34,640
Everyone, can I have ten seconds of your time?

111
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:36,760
To this special night.

112
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,040
All drinks tonight,

113
00:05:38,040 --> 00:05:39,240
on Mr. Ing.

114
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:42,120
Bangkok, make some noise.

115
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,440
In this world,

116
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,760
the winner takes it all,

117
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,360
and I...

118
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:56,800
am that winner.

119
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,400
It's all in the wrist, not the arm.

120
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:14,360
Like this?

121
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,520
Yeah, but you need a bit more arc.

122
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:17,560
Let me try.

123
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:38,799
P'Ing?

124
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,360
Are you okay?

125
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:58,120
P'Ing...

126
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,120
Are you alright?

127
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,040
I'm fine.

128
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,800
Be more careful next time.

129
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:04,840
We're sorry.

130
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,560
Who's this?

131
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,440
This is my friend, Yok,

132
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:12,160
Minister Pongpaisan's son.

133
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:16,240
Hello.

134
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:20,120
He's the one I told you about.

135
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:21,600
He just got back to Thailand this year.

136
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:23,360
We've known each other since we were kids.

137
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,920
How come I've never seen him before?

138
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,720
I'm older than you, then.

139
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:48,840
P'Ing.

140
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,000
What's all this?

141
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:03,520
You think this house is a basketball court?

142
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,720
You're soaking wet.

143
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:07,160
Let's take this conversation inside.

144
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:14,680
Come on, Yok.

145
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,320
You're drenched in sweat.

146
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:28,960
Aren't you afraid of catching a cold in the AC?

147
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,400
I'll turn it up.

148
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:37,960
Are you two alone? Where's Auntie Aoi?

149
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:39,800
She went to the market with Mom and Dad.

150
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,760
I mean, my mom.

151
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:42,960
They'll be back soon.

152
00:10:45,560 --> 00:10:46,240
Well,

153
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:48,240
aren't you hungry after the game? I'm starving.

154
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:49,480
What do you want to eat?

155
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,280
Anything. Just go whip something up.

156
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:53,120
Okay.

157
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,840
I'll go check the kitchen.

158
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:56,480
Be right back.

159
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:03,920
Hey.

160
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,600
What are you standing there for?

161
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:08,520
Come sit here.

162
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:29,520
Want a drag?

163
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:31,920
No, thanks.

164
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:35,480
Your name is Yok?

165
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:38,720
Cute name. Sounds like a girl's name.

166
00:11:41,480 --> 00:11:43,600
So, you're Phet Pongpruet's younger brother?

167
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,800
You know my brother?

168
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:52,920
How could I not know the youngest senator?

169
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,800
If the younger brother is this intriguing,

170
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:59,080
I wonder how interesting the older one must be.

171
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:04,760
To be honest, I'd really like to meet him.

172
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,800
Could you set us up if you have some time?

173
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:08,880
Maybe we'll hit it off better

174
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,320
since we're around the same age.

175
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,640
I'll let him know when I get the chance.

176
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,360
You catch on pretty quickly.

177
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:25,040
-I'd better go help out in the kitchen. -Hold on.

178
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:28,920
Where are you going?

179
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:30,560
Just sit down.

180
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:34,800
Let him cook. You're the guest here.

181
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,480
I have a few things to ask you.

182
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,520
Where do you go to school?

183
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:45,320
-Same college as Itt. -I see.

184
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:46,480
Impressive.

185
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:47,800
What's your major?

186
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:50,400
Political Science in International Relations.

187
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,920
Wow.

188
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:54,080
No wonder

189
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,560
you seem more composed than Itt.

190
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:57,200
Let me ask you something.

191
00:12:58,760 --> 00:13:00,080
Is Itt dating someone?

192
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:03,120
I've never heard him mention anyone.

193
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,760
Really?

194
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:07,600
You might have seen someone with him.

195
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,960
There must be tons of girls

196
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:10,840
throwing themselves at him.

197
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:13,120
Our faculties are quite far apart.

198
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,320
We don't cross paths that often.

199
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:16,200
What about you?

200
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:19,960
Are you dating someone?

201
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,320
I'm not interested in those kinds of things.

202
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,160
How is that even possible?

203
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:31,200
You're a college student. You're supposed to be dating.

204
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:32,960
Let's make a deal.

205
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:34,640
If Itt is seeing someone,

206
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:35,520
let me know.

207
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,400
I don't think he is.

208
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,840
If he were, he would have told me.

209
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:44,800
So, are you dating someone?

210
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,040
I'm not.

211
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:53,480
Leave it to me.

212
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,040
Just wait here.

213
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:04,360
Oh, Yok. You're here?

214
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:06,160
-Hello. -Hello.

215
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,760
Welcome, dear.

216
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,400
Sorry. The traffic was a nightmare.

217
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:10,920
That's why we're getting back so late.

218
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:11,960
It's no problem at all.

219
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:13,880
Don't be a stranger, Yok.

220
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:16,640
Make yourself at home.

221
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,560
Honey, you two chat for a bit.

222
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:20,200
I'll go see how things are in the kitchen.

223
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,600
How have you been? When did you get back?

224
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:23,640
-Just recently. -Oh, really?

225
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:26,720
Wow, you really went all out with the makeup.

226
00:14:39,040 --> 00:14:40,080
Those shrimp look delicious.

227
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:41,800
Let me peel them for you.

228
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:52,280
Here you go.

229
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:55,920
Itt, make sure you have some, too.

230
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:56,880
Yes, Mom.

231
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:03,840
Hey, Yok.

232
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:06,400
I had someone bring chamomile tea back from England.

233
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:08,680
Tell me if it's actually any good.

234
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,080
Sure thing.

235
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:11,280
Look.

236
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,600
Honey, could you bring the tea set over?

237
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,160
I'll go get it for you.

238
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,480
Careful, will you?

239
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,200
No matter how much money you have,

240
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:32,120
you can't buy another tea set like this.

241
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:35,520
Old things...

242
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:38,480
are always more valuable than anything new.

243
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,480
Don't you agree?

244
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,120
You're in luck today, Yok,

245
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:02,680
because this was my mom's tea set.

246
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:08,160
I'll brew the tea for you.

247
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:14,200
Thank you, P'Ing.

248
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,160
It smells great, Dad.

249
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:19,480
Itt,

250
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,440
your brother hasn't changed a bit

251
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:22,440
after all these years.

252
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:23,680
Arrogant as ever.

253
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:26,520
I even noticed another flaw today.

254
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,160
Opportunistic.

255
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:29,880
The second he saw me,

256
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:31,520
he started asking about my brother.

257
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:36,200
Compared to when we were kids,

258
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:37,840
he's actually being nice to me now.

259
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,040
He really is.

260
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:42,880
You're way too gullible.

261
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,160
Didn't you see

262
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,920
how he was bossing you around today?

263
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:50,960
It's probably just because my mom was there.

264
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:53,600
Why does he have to boss you and your mom around?

265
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,680
Things between me and my brother are complicated,

266
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:04,920
and I don't want my issues

267
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,359
to make you hate him.

268
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,160
Fine.

269
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,720
I'll try not to hate him, then.

270
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:12,200
Thanks.

271
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:16,839
I was planning to talk to him about wanting to...

272
00:17:21,359 --> 00:17:23,040
Hey, what are you guys talking about?

273
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:26,920
Oh, we were talking about heading back to the dorm,

274
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,160
figuring out what we should pack.

275
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:28,800
I see.

276
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:31,560
If you're done talking,

277
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,720
come on, I'll drive you.

278
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:33,400
Sound good?

279
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:39,120
That's okay, I don't want to waste your time.

280
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,400
Uncle Mhm can take us.

281
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:43,360
Uncle Mhm is getting old.

282
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,680
Let him spend some time with his family.

283
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:45,840
I'll take you myself.

284
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:53,440
It's just that...

285
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:56,640
we wanted to take a shower first.

286
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:59,080
We're all sweaty after playing basketball.

287
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:01,040
Oh, go ahead.

288
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:01,800
I'll wait.

289
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:03,240
Try to be quick, though.

290
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:04,920
Traffic is going to be terrible.

291
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,280
Then...

292
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,160
do you want to go first, or should I?

293
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,440
It's not that big of a deal.

294
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,080
You just shower in your own room.

295
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:17,840
As for Yok...

296
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:20,040
you can use mine.

297
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:23,840
Uh...

298
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:26,840
I don't think I can do that.

299
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:28,320
What do you mean?

300
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:30,840
Just use my bathroom.

301
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:32,720
It has everything you'll need.

302
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:34,400
We look to be about the same size, anyway.

303
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,240
Move it.

304
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,800
Waiting around is such a waste of time.

305
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:38,880
The traffic is already bad enough.

306
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:40,040
Hurry.

307
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:44,800
What are you waiting for? We need to beat the traffic.

308
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:46,680
Don't worry.

309
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:47,720
Just go shower in his room.

310
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:48,560
Go on.

311
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:50,120
Hurry.

312
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:07,160
Which one should I give him?

313
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:35,040
P'Ing?

314
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:36,920
Can you bring me a shirt?

315
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:49,880
Yeah.

316
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:07,720
Thank you, P'Ing.

317
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:12,560
I'll go wait downstairs.

318
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:14,240
Okay.

319
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:35,680
P'Ing,

320
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,480
are you free on the night of the 20th?

321
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:39,480
I'd like to take you out for dinner.

322
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:43,640
That's still a long way off.

323
00:20:44,360 --> 00:20:46,040
Ask me again when it gets closer.

324
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:54,560
Alright, I'll check with you again, then.

325
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:56,240
Get home safe.

326
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,840
I was planning to talk to him

327
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:08,480
about wanting to intern at Araya Group

328
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:10,720
so I can work hard and prove myself.

329
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:12,680
Maybe he'll start to see me in a better light.

330
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:13,920
Itt,

331
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,880
are you sure about this?

332
00:21:21,240 --> 00:21:22,320
Why are you still here?

333
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:25,280
My room is in the other building.

334
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,120
I see.

335
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:38,640
P'Ing,

336
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:41,000
the 20th is actually Itt's birthday.

337
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:43,120
He's been saving up his money for months.

338
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,360
If you aren't busy,

339
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,400
he really wants you to come to his party.

340
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:53,360
A college party?

341
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:54,960
Is that supposed to be fun?

342
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:02,080
Well...

343
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:05,560
will you be there?

344
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:07,880
Of course.

345
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:11,200
But Itt mentioned that...

346
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:12,240
he wants you

347
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:13,480
at his birthday party.

348
00:22:21,320 --> 00:22:23,440
Well, I'll give it some thought

349
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,600
because even you...

350
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,720
asked me for him.

351
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,120
I'm leaving, then.

352
00:22:37,440 --> 00:22:38,840
Hey, handsome Yok.

353
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:40,920
How's it going?

354
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:42,680
Damn, that car is sick.

355
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:44,320
-You look so good. -What are you wearing?

356
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:45,960
-It's not mine. -What kind of shirt is that?

357
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:47,960
I think you've gotten more handsome, though.

358
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:49,440
Wanna try acting in a BL series?

359
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:50,960
They're huge these days.

360
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:16,360
[Head Coach of Legend Muay Thai Camp, Dechkhun]

361
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,960
The "Perfect Face,"

362
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:21,600
Yok Pruttha,

363
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:24,000
is the winner.

364
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:26,840
Yok, can I have a word?

365
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,880
You showed real heart out there.

366
00:23:30,920 --> 00:23:32,320
Your punches were lightning fast.

367
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:34,760
It'd be a real waste if you didn't go pro.

368
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:36,280
If you want to see the real deal,

369
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:37,720
come find me anytime.

370
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:38,960
I'm a professional coach.

371
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:45,960
Nonsense.

372
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:48,840
What you need to be...

373
00:23:49,080 --> 00:23:51,720
is the one who makes the rules, not follows them.

374
00:23:51,840 --> 00:23:53,080
I brought you here

375
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:55,320
to help me maintain my reputation.

376
00:23:55,360 --> 00:23:57,000
Don't get too carried away with it.

377
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:11,040
[Head Coach of Legend Muay Thai Camp, Dechkhun]

378
00:24:53,520 --> 00:24:54,240
Hey.

379
00:24:55,520 --> 00:24:56,320
Yes?

380
00:24:58,280 --> 00:24:59,480
Bring that person over to me.

381
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:00,480
Sure.

382
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:10,720
Toss it.

383
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:13,320
-Go on, toss it. -Give it to me.

384
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:23,440
Sweet.

385
00:25:27,080 --> 00:25:27,760
Hey, stop running...

386
00:25:27,800 --> 00:25:29,800
-You're hopeless. Come on, check. -Bring it. Let's go.

387
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:31,840
-P'Ing, you actually came? -Wait up.

388
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:41,880
You're here?

389
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:44,600
Well, it is Itt's birthday, isn't it?

390
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:46,080
I wanted to see

391
00:25:46,120 --> 00:25:47,800
how kids party these days.

392
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:51,000
It's nothing you haven't seen before.

393
00:25:51,160 --> 00:25:52,840
Itt booked that place you like.

394
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:57,640
Shall we head out, then?

395
00:25:58,760 --> 00:25:59,360
Yeah.

396
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:04,200
Let's go.

397
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:14,160
Come on, everyone.

398
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:15,280
-Look, the cake's here. -Come on.

399
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:16,600
Let's blow out the candles.

400
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:23,120
Here it is.

401
00:26:23,720 --> 00:26:25,840
-Where's the lighter? -I'll go ask for one.

402
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:26,600
Okay.

403
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:28,400
Excited?

404
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:30,160
-The cake looks great. -Totally.

405
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:32,000
-Right? I want the strawberry. -Which piece do you want?

406
00:26:32,200 --> 00:26:33,840
I'll take the white one in the center.

407
00:26:33,880 --> 00:26:35,280
-Whoa. -That is sour, you know.

408
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:36,240
How do you know?

409
00:26:36,760 --> 00:26:38,040
White strawberries are usually sour.

410
00:26:39,080 --> 00:26:40,840
One, two, three.

411
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:43,840
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

412
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:46,400
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

413
00:26:46,760 --> 00:26:49,600
♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪

414
00:26:49,880 --> 00:26:53,840
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

415
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:54,920
Make a wish.

416
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:58,720
Cut it.

417
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:01,080
If you cut the cake unevenly, you're ruined.

418
00:27:01,840 --> 00:27:02,720
This one's for you, P'Ing.

419
00:27:02,960 --> 00:27:03,760
Just put it over there.

420
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:05,760
-This cake looks delicious, though. -Yeah.

421
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:12,080
-Yok, thanks for coming. -Don't let there be a third time.

422
00:27:12,400 --> 00:27:13,760
No need to thank me.

423
00:27:13,760 --> 00:27:15,160
We're friends. Of course I'd come.

424
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:16,600
Happy Birthday, Itt.

425
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:17,960
Thanks, man.

426
00:27:19,400 --> 00:27:20,560
Where's mine?

427
00:27:21,160 --> 00:27:23,360
Mine... For Nott and me.

428
00:27:24,760 --> 00:27:25,440
Why?

429
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:28,280
Your strawberry looks way more appetizing.

430
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:37,120
Hey, let's go dance.

431
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:38,520
-Yeah. -Come on, let's dance.

432
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:40,040
-Let's go. -Come on.

433
00:27:40,080 --> 00:27:41,240
I'm heading out now.

434
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,000
Wait, P'Ing.

435
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:45,720
-We just started. -Do you want me to just stand here?

436
00:27:45,960 --> 00:27:47,080
Enjoy yourselves.

437
00:27:47,440 --> 00:27:48,760
I'll take care of the tab.

438
00:27:49,360 --> 00:27:50,880
I'll see you out, then.

439
00:27:50,880 --> 00:27:51,640
No need.

440
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:56,480
Let's go dance.

441
00:28:03,160 --> 00:28:03,880
P'Ing...

442
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:07,360
You forgot your lighter.

443
00:28:08,280 --> 00:28:08,960
Oh...

444
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:15,640
Thanks a lot.

445
00:28:19,280 --> 00:28:20,200
Are you not having fun?

446
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:23,000
Not really.

447
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:25,040
Itt sure has a lot of friends, doesn't he?

448
00:28:26,080 --> 00:28:26,840
Yeah, he does.

449
00:28:29,560 --> 00:28:30,480
Yok,

450
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:32,440
are you his best friend?

451
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,360
We've been playing together since we were kids.

452
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:36,840
We kept in touch even when we weren't together.

453
00:28:38,360 --> 00:28:40,080
How come Itt never told me that?

454
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:44,120
Well, you aren't exactly with him all the time.

455
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:47,520
You have a point.

456
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:49,920
He doesn't need to

457
00:28:49,920 --> 00:28:51,040
tell his brother everything.

458
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:53,840
Bye.

459
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:09,240
Yeah?

460
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,160
Today is Itt's birthday,

461
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:14,320
but you haven't wished him a happy birthday yet.

462
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:15,440
Hey.

463
00:29:19,120 --> 00:29:21,520
I already went over and even smiled at him.

464
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:23,440
Still not satisfied?

465
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:27,760
Itt has looked up to you since he was a kid.

466
00:29:28,640 --> 00:29:30,520
If you wished him a happy birthday,

467
00:29:31,160 --> 00:29:33,200
it would mean more to him than anything else.

468
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:34,000
Wait a minute.

469
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:35,400
He's looked up to me?

470
00:29:38,600 --> 00:29:40,600
To be honest, Itt and I...

471
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:42,400
are not typical brothers.

472
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:46,000
You're his older brother.

473
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:48,800
Can't you try to be nicer to him?

474
00:29:49,520 --> 00:29:53,720
Oh, so you're saying a simple "Happy Birthday" is...

475
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:55,720
all it takes to be nice?

476
00:30:00,320 --> 00:30:01,320
Alright, then.

477
00:30:01,520 --> 00:30:02,360
I'll do it.

478
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:04,880
Just a "Happy Birthday," right?

479
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:07,480
-Yes. -Do you want me to sing the whole song?

480
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:14,040
Please just do it.

481
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:32,760
Alright, let's go.

482
00:30:33,360 --> 00:30:34,520
Time to have some fun.

483
00:30:35,120 --> 00:30:38,480
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

484
00:30:38,880 --> 00:30:42,520
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

485
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:01,480
Happy Birthday.

486
00:31:03,440 --> 00:31:04,920
Thank you, P'Ing.

487
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:07,160
Okay.

488
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:09,920
Go on, have fun with your friends.

489
00:31:24,080 --> 00:31:25,160
Hey, handsome.

490
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:26,600
First time here?

491
00:31:28,200 --> 00:31:29,120
Don't touch me.

492
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:31,360
Did you just shake me off?

493
00:31:33,040 --> 00:31:35,200
-Hey, Jason. -Bring it.

494
00:31:35,880 --> 00:31:37,760
-Ing, good thing you're here. -Jason...

495
00:31:37,800 --> 00:31:39,840
-Jason, it's just me. -Yok...

496
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:41,280
Hey, take it easy.

497
00:31:41,680 --> 00:31:42,680
Calm down.

498
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:44,280
I'm glad you're here.

499
00:31:44,320 --> 00:31:45,480
-This kid is asking for trouble... -Whoa, whoa.

500
00:31:45,520 --> 00:31:47,720
Jason, listen.

501
00:31:48,440 --> 00:31:51,440
Go order some drinks. It's on me.

502
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:52,560
Fine.

503
00:31:53,280 --> 00:31:54,640
Are you alright?

504
00:31:55,360 --> 00:31:56,160
I am.

505
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:15,120
I'm sorry. It's my fault for picking this place.

506
00:32:16,120 --> 00:32:17,040
It's not your fault.

507
00:32:20,440 --> 00:32:21,920
Why do you like this place so much?

508
00:32:23,800 --> 00:32:24,840
It belongs to a friend of mine,

509
00:32:25,240 --> 00:32:26,480
so I come here quite often.

510
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:29,600
It's usually this packed during Pride Month.

511
00:32:29,800 --> 00:32:31,480
By the way, did you forget something?

512
00:32:32,440 --> 00:32:33,760
I just helped you out back there.

513
00:32:34,040 --> 00:32:35,360
You haven't even thanked me yet.

514
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:39,400
Thank you, P'Ing.

515
00:32:39,880 --> 00:32:41,360
Actually, P'Ing...

516
00:32:42,080 --> 00:32:43,360
It's my birthday today.

517
00:32:43,640 --> 00:32:44,200
Yeah?

518
00:32:44,800 --> 00:32:46,240
I already wished you a Happy Birthday.

519
00:32:47,400 --> 00:32:48,680
I want a birthday present.

520
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:51,640
You're making demands now?

521
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:55,800
Can I intern at your company during the break?

522
00:32:56,600 --> 00:32:58,080
Yok wants to go, too.

523
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:03,240
He won't be able to handle it.

524
00:33:04,280 --> 00:33:06,120
If I work him too hard,

525
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:07,840
his brother will probably rip me a new one.

526
00:33:09,640 --> 00:33:10,840
I've already spoken with P'Phet.

527
00:33:11,840 --> 00:33:13,600
He wants me to learn the ropes from you.

528
00:33:16,680 --> 00:33:17,920
Are you sure you're up for it?

529
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,640
My standards are incredibly high.

530
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:22,760
I don't have a problem with that.

531
00:33:24,160 --> 00:33:25,080
What about you, Yok?

532
00:33:27,160 --> 00:33:28,160
No problem at all.

533
00:33:32,560 --> 00:33:33,760
Then it's settled.

534
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:37,640
Really? Thank you so much, P'Ing.

535
00:33:38,320 --> 00:33:40,200
This is the best birthday present ever.

536
00:33:40,920 --> 00:33:42,080
Itt, come dance with us.

537
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:43,680
The music is fire. Come on.

538
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:45,600
-Let's go. -Come on.

539
00:33:46,080 --> 00:33:48,120
Check this out, a moonwalk.

540
00:33:55,800 --> 00:33:58,360
The traffic was going to be awful,

541
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:00,120
so I left early, Secretary Piang.

542
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:02,840
Don't worry about it.

543
00:34:04,680 --> 00:34:06,280
I'll find my way back home somehow.

544
00:34:07,560 --> 00:34:08,239
Okay.

545
00:34:19,360 --> 00:34:20,679
What was I thinking?

546
00:34:22,760 --> 00:34:24,800
As if coming here means I'll get to see him.

547
00:34:39,560 --> 00:34:40,360
P'Ing?

548
00:34:44,360 --> 00:34:45,239
It's really hot out here,

549
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:47,719
so I went to wash my face.

550
00:34:48,440 --> 00:34:49,040
Yeah.

551
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:50,960
It is hot.

552
00:34:52,639 --> 00:34:54,440
Why are you still here, though?

553
00:34:56,239 --> 00:34:57,600
I'm playing basketball with my friends.

554
00:34:57,600 --> 00:34:59,520
What brings you here?

555
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,080
I'm looking for Itt.

556
00:35:05,480 --> 00:35:07,320
He doesn't have any classes today.

557
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:09,960
Oh, is that so?

558
00:35:13,240 --> 00:35:14,840
-Uh... -Yok, you still in for more?

559
00:35:14,920 --> 00:35:15,520
Of course.

560
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:18,520
-Oh, it's P'Ing. -Hey.

561
00:35:18,520 --> 00:35:20,600
Hey, P'Ing. Hi.

562
00:35:20,640 --> 00:35:21,640
-Hi. -Wanna play some ball?

563
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:23,320
We're one short for a three-on-three.

564
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:24,000
What?

565
00:35:24,320 --> 00:35:26,120
Phum just went home to his mom.

566
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:28,800
-I'm in. -In that outfit?

567
00:35:29,440 --> 00:35:30,120
Why?

568
00:35:33,280 --> 00:35:34,320
Are you worried about me?

569
00:35:36,720 --> 00:35:37,320
Let's go.

570
00:35:39,360 --> 00:35:40,160
He's actually pretty good.

571
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:52,640
In those shoes and pants, are you sure?

572
00:35:53,120 --> 00:35:53,880
Why?

573
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:55,760
Are you worried about me?

574
00:35:58,040 --> 00:35:59,160
If you don't take this seriously,

575
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:01,120
you're going to lose.

576
00:36:05,800 --> 00:36:06,680
Was that a fluke?

577
00:36:07,440 --> 00:36:09,040
Didn't Itt ever tell you...

578
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:12,560
I used to be a basketball player?

579
00:36:20,440 --> 00:36:21,120
Let's do this.

580
00:36:22,520 --> 00:36:24,160
He's a has-been pro.

581
00:36:31,640 --> 00:36:33,360
Nice shot.

582
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:34,400
Did you see that?

583
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:37,360
That was clean. Nice shot.

584
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:39,600
Nice.

585
00:36:40,280 --> 00:36:41,240
Nice.

586
00:36:45,960 --> 00:36:46,880
Come on.

587
00:36:51,680 --> 00:36:52,600
Go for it.

588
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:10,960
-You've actually got moves. -Nice.

589
00:37:21,560 --> 00:37:22,400
Come on.

590
00:37:49,120 --> 00:37:50,040
Hey, P'Ing.

591
00:37:50,040 --> 00:37:50,840
-You okay? -Are you hurt?

592
00:37:50,880 --> 00:37:52,320
P'Ing, let's get you up.

593
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:53,400
My leg, Yok...

594
00:37:53,400 --> 00:37:54,080
Are you alright?

595
00:37:54,400 --> 00:37:55,800
-Are you okay? -Yeah, I'm fine.

596
00:38:02,680 --> 00:38:03,680
Easy.

597
00:38:04,360 --> 00:38:04,920
Hey.

598
00:38:04,960 --> 00:38:07,000
Aren't you only in your early 20s?

599
00:38:07,640 --> 00:38:08,640
Playing basketball always...

600
00:38:08,680 --> 00:38:10,080
Damn, it's so red.

601
00:38:11,320 --> 00:38:12,640
Does anyone have some water?

602
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:14,600
How are you feeling, P'Ing?

603
00:38:15,760 --> 00:38:16,560
I think...

604
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:18,760
once you get older,

605
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:20,760
if you don't stretch, this is what happens.

606
00:38:21,560 --> 00:38:23,600
Aren't you only in your 20s?

607
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:25,800
You're bound to get a few scrapes.

608
00:38:25,840 --> 00:38:27,600
Aren't you overthinking it?

609
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:29,720
Here, Yok.

610
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:31,520
Take it.

611
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:37,800
I'm sorry, P'Ing.

612
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:45,640
With your left leg injured like this,

613
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:47,320
how are you going to drive back?

614
00:38:48,080 --> 00:38:48,960
I'll be fine.

615
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:52,920
I can handle it.

616
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:57,280
Why did you do that?

617
00:38:58,760 --> 00:38:59,960
I don't think you can drive.

618
00:39:04,200 --> 00:39:06,960
Give me the keys. I'll drive you home.

619
00:39:26,840 --> 00:39:27,920
Yok, let me be blunt.

620
00:39:28,400 --> 00:39:29,240
I'm being serious.

621
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:31,480
Damn, your driving is just...

622
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:33,600
an absolute nightmare.

623
00:39:33,640 --> 00:39:35,200
Where did you learn that from?

624
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:39,920
Hey.

625
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:42,120
Not going to answer?

626
00:39:44,160 --> 00:39:45,160
Put me down here.

627
00:39:53,480 --> 00:39:54,360
What are you smiling about?

628
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:57,200
It's nothing.

629
00:40:03,680 --> 00:40:05,200
I'm hungry.

630
00:40:06,600 --> 00:40:07,840
I'm starving.

631
00:40:11,160 --> 00:40:13,000
Surprise.

632
00:40:13,080 --> 00:40:15,320
There's nothing in the fridge.

633
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:17,320
Don't you usually cook for yourself?

634
00:40:17,440 --> 00:40:18,880
Why would I bother if I live alone?

635
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:20,160
I just order in.

636
00:40:23,560 --> 00:40:26,080
There's some instant noodles. Want me to make some?

637
00:40:26,880 --> 00:40:27,640
Yeah.

638
00:40:28,360 --> 00:40:30,040
Whatever you make, I'll eat it.

639
00:40:40,280 --> 00:40:40,960
Yok,

640
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:43,880
help me get to the bathroom.

641
00:40:44,320 --> 00:40:45,080
It's upstairs.

642
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:49,760
Okay.

643
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:54,280
Easy... My ankle really hurts.

644
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:04,280
Back in the day...

645
00:41:06,160 --> 00:41:07,600
I used to play basketball all the time,

646
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:10,720
but once I started working, there was...

647
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:16,480
There was hardly any time left.

648
00:41:17,560 --> 00:41:18,800
Do I still have the moves?

649
00:41:21,520 --> 00:41:22,320
Yes, you do.

650
00:41:48,200 --> 00:41:49,280
Give me a hand here.

651
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:51,880
I'm going to take my pants off.

652
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:02,400
Yok,

653
00:42:02,600 --> 00:42:04,040
help me get to the bathroom.

654
00:42:04,400 --> 00:42:05,080
Did you know...

655
00:42:05,120 --> 00:42:06,240
building a body like this...

656
00:42:06,280 --> 00:42:07,800
takes more than just working out?

657
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:08,840
Put Itt

658
00:42:08,880 --> 00:42:10,120
in Corporate Development.

659
00:42:10,280 --> 00:42:12,040
As for Yok, you'll be my personal assistant.

660
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:13,720
Today is extremely important.

661
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:15,400
We need to close this deal at any cost.

662
00:42:15,400 --> 00:42:16,560
Normally...

663
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:18,120
aren't you someone

664
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:20,280
who can separate work from personal life?

665
00:42:20,320 --> 00:42:22,680
Taking care of my boss is part of my job.
